# Build context for Dockerfile.web (context is the repo root, since a Flutter
# web build needs pubspec, lib/, assets/ and web/ together).
#
# Everything excluded here would otherwise be uploaded to the Docker daemon on
# every build. The Gradle and Dart caches alone run to several GB and are
# useless to a web build — they are the difference between a context that
# transfers in seconds and one that takes minutes before the first layer runs.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The compose .env holds the database password, JWT secret and SMTP
# credentials. It reaches containers as environment variables and must never
# be copied into an image layer, where anyone able to pull the image can read
# it — including from an earlier layer after a later one deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.docker.example
**/key.properties
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore

# ── Build output and caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
.dart_tool/
.pub-cache/
.pub/
**/.gradle/
android/app/debug/
android/app/profile/
android/app/release/

# ── Platform targets a web build never reads ─────────────────────────────────
android/
ios/
linux/
macos/
windows/

# ── The backend, which has its own image and its own .dockerignore ───────────
backend/

# ── Repository and tooling metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# ── Tests and docs: not part of a production bundle ──────────────────────────
test/
*.md
